WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.901
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.601
You're here. You're watching.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:07.667
You made it. You all look good.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.701
Well, guys, we had a great lead-in tonight.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.701
We're following the January 6th hearing.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.767
So...you guys ready for some comedy?

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:17.100
That's right. Earlier tonight, Congress held the first

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.834
public hearing on the January 6th attack,

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:22.634
and it aired in prime time across all major networks.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.901
Yep. The footage is rough to get through.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.567
Right after the hearing, I watched an episode

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.067
of "Dateline" just to lighten the mood.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.601
Five minutes in, even Mike Pence was like, "I've had enough.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:34.067
Let's see what's happening on 'RuPaul's Drag Race.'"

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:36.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.200
Yep, they're saying each hearing could run anywhere

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.033
from 90 minutes to 2 1/2 hours.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.300
Yeah, it's strange --

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.767
one minute you're watching the hearing,

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.300
the next, it's "American Ninja Warrior."

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.868
And so it's -- you're basically going from people scaling walls

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:50.000
to people...scaling walls.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.400
Yeah, all the major networks are airing the hearings,

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.701
but Fox News isn't.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:54.968
[ Audience ohs ]

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.968
Instead, they're showing reruns of January 6th

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.200
with a laugh track.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.767
I don't think that's -- They should --

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:05.634
That's right -- Tonight, NBC, CBS, ABC, MSNBC, and CNN

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:08.267
all showed the first hearing, but Fox News didn't.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.501
Apparently, they didn't think it was newsworthy.

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:13.133
Let's see what they were focused on instead.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.200
-Tonight on Fox News...

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.667
is the new Wendy's pink Frosty trying to turn your kids gay?

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:19.901
-Wow. That's...

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:22.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.467
[ Applause ]

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.968
They find that newsworthy.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.801
Some more news out of Washington.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.667
I read that President Biden has been dealing with

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.968
a rapid turnover of his staff.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.667
Yeah, of course, the White House tried to spin it like,

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.300
"Hey, look at all the new jobs the President is creating."

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.033
Yeah, things are tough at the White House.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.767
Today Biden was like, "Hey, Jill, can you believe

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.234
how many people are lea--

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:47.300
Jill? Jill?"

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.801
Well, this is fun.

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:51.100
Uber released their annual Lost and Found Index,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.133
which reveals the items reported lost by passengers.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:57.100
Glasses, phones, keys were some of the more common ones.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.501
But get this -- five people left behind --

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.000
They left behind their dentures.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.934
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.834
Apparently some people like to go for a ride because they love

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:06.767
the feel of the wind in their gums.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.133
Yep, people have left glasses, teeth,

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:13.000
and even a Bernie Sanders fanny pack.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.801
In other words, Bernie Sanders lost a bunch of personal items.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.367
[ Laughter ] Have you guys seen this?

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.367
There's a new trend on TikTok where people

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:21.567
are making "healthy Coke" by mixing

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:24.167
flavored sparkling water with balsamic vinegar.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.734
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.701
Yeah, it really shows you the lengths Coke drinkers

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:30.467
will go to avoid Pepsi, don't you think?

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.167
Yeah, on a hot day, there's nothing more refreshing

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:34.901
than 32 ounces of salad dressing.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.234
Some entertainment news.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:37.667
The Hallmark Channel just announced

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:40.501
that their 2022 Christmas in July event

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:41.701
is going to premiere

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:44.133
three new original Hallmark Christmas movies.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.000
[ Cheers and applause ] Yeah.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.234
I love it.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.901
-Wait. Christmas? in July?

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:53.100
Psssh. I don't have time for that.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.634
-What are you talking about, Tariq?

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:56.901
There's always time for Hallmark Christmas movies,

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:59.033
no matter what time of year it is.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.300
-No, Jimmy, there isn't.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.734
I mean, you know how important my other career is to me.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:07.334
-You mean your family's wooden toy-making business?

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.934
-Exactly!

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:11.901
And ever since I became CEO,

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:14.601
I've just been under a lot of pressure, you know?

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:17.534
There's just too many toys to sell!

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.667
Plus, you know I'm the chairman of my hometown's

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.234
big annual Nutcracker Festival,

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.667
and I still need to find a venue!

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:27.534
-Wow. I had no idea that you were under so much pressure.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.267
-Yeah, well, I am.

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.501
And to top it off, Mayor Santa's expecting me

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:35.200
to make a big Christmas in July charity donation

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.300
at the kickoff -- party.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.067
♪♪

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:47.033
-The kickoff -- The kickoff party?

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.634
-Well, yeah! -Alright.

00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:51.868
Well, Tariq, I think the answer might be closer than you think.

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:54.300
W-W-What's that on your bandstand?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.234
♪♪

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:00.801
-It's a wooden nutcracker!

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.267
That's it!

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.300
We'll -- We'll hold the big annual

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.234
Nutcracker Festival kickoff party

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.734
at my family's wooden toy factory!

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:11.367
And then just donate all our extra toys to charity!

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:15.000
Jimmy, you just saved Christmas in July.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:19.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.300
♪♪

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.133
-Will you marry me?

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.667
-What the [bleep]?

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.501
♪♪

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:34.968
[ Steve laughing ]

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:37.467
-"Kickoff party."

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.000
-Yeah.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.133
He didn't know how he was gonna do it at the kickoff.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.300
-Yeah. -Party.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.767
Guys, I heard about a man who's suing American Airlines

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:52.734
after they mistakenly gave his name to police

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:54.934
in connection with a robbery at an airport shop

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.334
and he spent 17 days in jail.

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:58.667
Yeah.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.901
Even worse, since going from American Airlines to prison

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:03.434
was an upgrade, he was also charged for it.

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:04.868
Hey. Listen to this.

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:07.434
A man in Florida was bitten by a 7-foot alligator

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:11.133
after mistaking it for a dog with a long leash.

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:12.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.334
Unfortunately, he was bitten again when he tried calling 911

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.467
on a raccoon he thought was a phone, yeah.

